{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790725963,"nonce":"so4hVdr+WHyTPWRDdn2GYQLcNvY=","title":"OSR callback registries hold RwLock guards across compilation","message":"The lazy compiler, lazy optimizer, promotion requester, and optimizing-install hook invoke their registered callbacks while retaining the global registry RwLock read guard.\n\nThose callbacks can decode snapshot bodies, run the HIR pipeline, compile Cranelift or LLVM code, and spawn or install resume points. Native futex stack attribution on the NUC reached set_lazy_compiler and the lazy callback path while first-call compilation was active. A concurrent runtime setup or callback replacement waits for the whole compile, and callback re-entry into its registry can deadlock.\n\nClone an Arc to the callback while holding the guard, drop the guard, and invoke the clone. Keep the maps and queue locks limited to their short metadata operations.","files":null}]}